/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 58 0 R
/T (Perovskite solar cells \(PSCs\) have achieved efficiencies \(~28%\) comparable to those of conventional silicon solar cells in a short span of time. However, it is difficult for them to compete with the well-established Si solar cell market. Therefore, PSCs need to target niche markets where conventional Si cells may lag. Being compatible with flexible applications, PSCs offer advantages over conventional cells in markets such as building-integrated photovoltaics \(BIPV\), wearable electronics, transportation and aviation, IoTs, etc.)
/E (Perovskite solar cells \(PSCs\) have achieved efficiencies \(~28%\) comparable to those of conventional silicon solar cells in a short span of time. However, it is difficult for them to compete with the well-established Si solar cell market. Therefore, PSCs need to target niche markets where conventional Si cells may lag. Being compatible with flexible applications, PSCs offer advantages over conventional cells in markets such as building-integrated photovoltaics \(BIPV\), wearable electronics, transportation and aviation, IoTs, etc.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
103 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 58 0 R
/T (In this work, steel is used as a substrate for fabricating PSCs. A thin metal layer is utilized to form the semi-transparent top conducting contact. For the bottom contact, an Al/Ti electrode is explored, which offers a cost-effective solution compared to the conventionally used expensive gold contact. Additionally, it offers better wettability for the subsequent layer used in the cell architecture. This work demonstrates a record cell efficiency of 8.31% for this cell configuration.)
/E (In this work, steel is used as a substrate for fabricating PSCs. A thin metal layer is utilized to form the semi-transparent top conducting contact. For the bottom contact, an Al/Ti electrode is explored, which offers a cost-effective solution compared to the conventionally used expensive gold contact. Additionally, it offers better wettability for the subsequent layer used in the cell architecture. This work demonstrates a record cell efficiency of 8.31% for this cell configuration.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
