270 0 obj
<<
/Title (In this work, steel is used as a substrate for fabricating PSCs. A thin metal layer is utilized to form the semi-transparent top conducting contact. For the bottom contact, an Al/Ti electrode is explored, which offers a cost-effective solution compared to the conventionally used expensive gold contact. Additionally, it offers better wettability for the subsequent layer used in the cell architecture. This work demonstrates a record cell efficiency of 8.31% for this cell configuration.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 308 0 R
/Next 213 0 R
>>
