/Title (Perovskite solar cells \(PSCs\) have achieved efficiencies \(~28%\) comparable to those of conventional silicon solar cells in a short span of time. However, it is difficult for them to compete with the well-established Si solar cell market. Therefore, PSCs need to target niche markets where conventional Si cells may lag. Being compatible with flexible applications, PSCs offer advantages over conventional cells in markets such as building-integrated photovoltaics \(BIPV\), wearable electronics, transportation and aviation, IoTs, etc.)
